      "content_summary": "Addresses service unresponsiveness and 503 errors in Deploy Manager caused by bad deployments or resource exhaustion, outlining immediate rollback and capacity scaling steps.",
      "content_body": "When a specific Deploy Manager instance returns 503 errors or is reported as partially unavailable, first check the recent deployment history for potential bad releases. If a recent change correlates with the onset of issues, perform an immediate rollback to the last stable version. If no recent deployment occurred, inspect resource metrics for CPU or memory exhaustion, which often triggers these availability drops. For resource exhaustion, temporarily increase capacity or adjust rate limits to stabilize the service while investigating long-term optimization or applying the latest product patch."
